  ============================================================================
  Dark Roast: Velvet — iTerm2 Color Scheme
  Version: 5.1.0 Companion

  WHAT IS THIS
  ——————
  A complete iTerm2 color scheme (.itermcolors) implementing the Dark Roast
  design system's ANSI-16 palette. Covers all 16 ANSI colors plus every iTerm2
  chrome key (background, foreground, cursor, selection, bold, badge, tab, link).

  INSTALL
  ———-
  Option A (easiest — double-click):
    1. Double-click "Dark Roast Velvet.itermcolors" in Finder
       (or: open "Dark Roast Velvet.itermcolors" from Terminal)
    2. iTerm2 will import it automatically under Preferences →
       Profiles → Colors → Color Presets → "Dark Roast Velvet"
    3. Select it from the Color Presets dropdown in your profile

  Option B (manual import):
    1. iTerm2 → Settings (⌘,) → Profiles → Colors
    2. Click "Color Presets..." dropdown → "Import..."
    3. Select this file
    4. Select "Dark Roast Velvet" from the Color Presets dropdown

  Option C (apply to all profiles):
    Import as above, then go to each profile and select the preset.
    To set as default for new sessions, update the "Default" profile.

  ABOUT THE FORMAT
  ————————
  iTerm2 stores colors as XML plists where each color is a dict with five keys:
    Alpha Component  — float 0.0–1.0  (1.0 = fully opaque)
    Blue Component   — float 0.0–1.0
    Color Space      — string ("sRGB" for standard, "P3" for wide-gamut)
    Green Component  — float 0.0–1.0
    Red Component    — float 0.0–1.0

  All Dark Roast colors are specified in sRGB. No P3 wide-gamut is used; the
  palette is designed for warm espresso tones, not high-saturation display-P3.

  PALETTE PHILOSOPHY
  —————————
  All four Dark Roast terminal themes (Warp, Tabby, Terminal.app, iTerm2)
  share an identical ANSI-16 palette so that ls, git diff, vim syntax,
  tmux, and every other CLI tool produce exactly the same output regardless
  of which emulator you're running in.

  FULL COLOR REFERENCE
  ——————————
  Chrome:
    background    #190605   void      — warm-dark deepest layer
    foreground    #F7EADE   crema     — primary text (16.62:1 contrast vs void)
    cursor        #42B3A8   teal      — kinetic cursor, matches editor caret
    cursor text   #190605   void      — text inside cursor block (inverted)
    selection bg  #3B1817   espresso  — warm polished surface (v4: was `grain`)
    selection fg  #F7EADE   crema     — text color on selection
    bold          #F7EADE   crema     — bold text color (same hue, higher weight)
    badge         #D4494E   scarlet   — iTerm2 badge/notification
    tab           #240A09   obsidian  — tab bar background color
    link          #42B3A8   teal      — hyperlink color in terminal output

  ANSI Normal (indices 0–7):
    0  black       #240A09   obsidian  — dark floor (not as deep as void)
    1  red         #D4494E   scarlet   — error / critical
    2  green       #60A659   sage      — warm fern (terminal extension)
    3  yellow      #E18826   amber     — warning / accent
    4  blue        #608BB7   slate     — dusty steel blue (terminal extension)
    5  magenta     #BC60AD   mauve     — dried lavender (terminal extension)
    6  cyan        #42B3A8   teal      — live data flow / resolved
    7  white       #E4D1C2   bone      — reduced-contrast light text

  ANSI Bright (indices 8–15):
    8  bright black    #AC8981   crater-deep — comment gray, tmux inactive (v4: was `crater`)
    9  bright red      #ED6667   scarlet+  — scarlet companion-bright
    10 bright green    #7EBE77   sage+     — sage companion-bright
    11 bright yellow   #E4AE28   gold      — success / stable severity
    12 bright blue     #77A3D0   slate+    — slate companion-bright
    13 bright magenta  #D47AC4   mauve+    — mauve companion-bright
    14 bright cyan     #63CDC1   teal+     — teal brightened (lighter than #42B3A8;
                                             bright should be visibly brighter)
    15 bright white    #F7EADE   crema     — full brightness
  ============================================================================
-->
